From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe14 <engine@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:24:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/21] frontend: Fire Emblem Fates' Choose your game page and
 Switch game (Seal of Flames)

A Fire Emblem Fates program (linked recompiled code starting Fates SE USA,
0004000000179800) with a window first shows "Choose your game": Fire Emblem
Fates (the default) or the optional fan mod Seal of Flames by Laz14
(gamebanana.com/mods/656034, CC BY-NC-ND 4.0), shown only when its profile
is installed, else greyed with an Install button that runs the port's
tools/play/sof.py install hidden (python -I, CREATE_NO_WINDOW, 10 min cap).
The last choice is remembered in game-choice.txt beside the program's folder
(never in settings.toml, never written headless) and pre-selected; Enter,
Start or A continues. The Esc menu gets Switch game, which asks first
("Unsaved progress will be lost") and then stops the game and starts the
other one in the same window: the same drop and loader::load that Reset
makes, with the other game's data folder and settings in between. Every
other program and game is unchanged.

Per choice (new module game_pick):
- Fire Emblem Fates keeps exactly today's data folder (--data, else the
  system's place) and settings: its Config is today's in every field.
- Seal of Flames plays from <profile>\data (saves, states, cheats, its mods
  folder, the log); the profile is --seal-profile, else FEF_SEAL_PROFILE,
  else seal-of-flames beside the program's folder. bring_saves is not run
  for it (it only copies ./user of old Zakuro builds into the normal folder).
- General settings stay shared (the owner's settings.toml); the game bits
  of the shared title id (per_game and enhancements) are kept apart in
  <profile>\game-settings.toml, seeded once from the round-52 profile's own
  settings or the port's first-run picks. While Seal plays, saves write the
  owner's file with his own game bits put back unchanged.
- The randomizer runs only for Fire Emblem Fates: Config::fates_rando (patch
  0011) is off for Seal, the Randomizer page's schema is not asked for and
  the Esc menu's Randomizer entry stays out.

Command line: --game fates|seal (pre-selects with a window, starts directly
headless), --seal-profile <dir>, --seal-broken (the launcher's full check
failed: shown as Needs repair). Headless with neither --game nor
FEF_GAME_CHOICE is Fire Emblem Fates and never reads the remembered file.
Test hooks (headless only, same code path): FEF_GAME_SWITCH_AT=frames calls
the same switch_game, replaying ZAKURO_REPLAY from its start at each boot;
FEF_HEADLESS_REPORT=file writes one JSON record per boot, switch and end
(choice, data folder, frames, fates_rando, sha256 of FEF_HEADLESS_RANGES,
also at FEF_HEADLESS_HASH_AT).

Checked: cargo test -p zakuro --lib, 88 passed, 2 ignored (9 new: CLI
pre-select, choice order and headless default, remembered file round trip,
installed by names only, page greying and controller, settings split keeps
the owner's game bits byte-equal, Seal bits round trip and seeding, hidden
install command, report ranges).
